   $q$In paragraph 1, bats "leave their roosts." What is a "roost"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a kind of insect","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"a loud squeak","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"a place where bats rest","is_correct":true},{"text":"a group of bats flying together","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a place where bats rest$q$, $q$The next sentence defines it: "A roost is a place where bats rest, such as a cave." Insects are what bats hunt, not where they rest.$q$, 'draft', 'b8d8f3f4-e7ab-57cb-b488-c6365d36ab3b')
